foreign  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  [Music]  when I was 23  I had just graduated from the University  of Hawaii with big hopes and dreams  started a career that would take me  Halfway Around the World  and I was in love  I was 14 years ago  and then everything seemed to fall apart  all at once  I was in the middle of a work shift at a  store in Honolulu when I picked up the  phone and heard my mom's voice on the  other end  and what she said brought my world to a  halt  my grandfather who is only 65 had  unexpectedly been given just two months  to live  [Music]  for the first eight years of my life  before my mom met and married my stepdad  my grandfather was the only father I  knew  it was hard to imagine a world without  him in it  in that moment over 4 000 miles of ocean  and land stretched between us  and  there I was  folding clothes when he had only two  months left to live  time seemed to both stop and speed up in  that moment  and everything else along with it  [Music]  [Music]  [Applause]  foreign  I asked my manager for a transfer to the  mainland and soon I had left everything  and everyone I knew for a place that was  completely foreign to me  Kentucky  but I wound up quitting so I could  travel to see my grandfather another  family who lived further south  and then I just kept on traveling for  months actually  pretty much until I ran out of money  at which point I went back to work for  the same company  at a shopping mall in Florence Kentucky  as the months went by I began to feel  stuck  I didn't have many friends in Kentucky  or direction or motivation  I didn't want to go out to the bars or  meet anyone new or move up at work  I just wanted to stay untethered  unattached uninvested in this place that  just didn't feel like home  so instead I would sit in my room  peppered with empty photo frames and  unopened boxes and watched the sunset  from my window  overlooking the street below  [Music]  the more beautiful The View it's like  the more unhappy I felt  and that might sound strange but  I just wanted so badly to be out there  experiencing it away from the city just  someplace Wild  [Music]  I miss my old life in Hawaii so much but  for some reason I felt like that life  was no longer Within Reach and that  maybe this was just My New Reality  and all the rest was just a dream  [Music]  it doesn't take long to lose sight of  your dreams  to trade curiosity for routine  which is exactly where I found myself  Frozen somewhere between life imagined  and the life I knew  when my brother gave me a book  he said this is you you should read it  that book was Into the Wild by John  krakar  [Music]  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Applause]  foreign  [Music]  some say that Chris McCandless story is  dangerous  careless misguided  and maybe it is a lot of stories are  but even for those who have adhered to a  life of caution and responsibility  the outcome is still the same  none of us make it out alive  the question I wonder is did you live  and if given the choice would you do it  all over again  ready three two one go  oh  I haven't jumped on a moving train or  burned piles of cash or abandoned my car  in the Mojave Desert to wander around on  foot  I haven't crossed solo into Mexico on a  river raft or journeyed alone through  the Alaskan wilderness  when my brother said this is you  I sometimes wonder if he meant you would  do this wouldn't you  what  but more than that I think you recognize  the side of me I didn't yet understand  the side of me that felt a kind of  restless discomfort and persistent  desire to live outside the lines  to make sense of things in my own way  through experience exploration and  Escape  maybe he guessed that one day it might  break me if I kept it all inside  and who knows maybe he would have been  right  there's a passage from the book that  really stuck with me it's this scene  where Chris catches a ride from a local  man named Ron back to his camp  Ron asks how old he is and Chris says  23.  23 years old says Ron don't you think  you ought to get an education and a job  and make something of this life  I've been asked a hundred variations of  this same question throughout my life  and even more so since choosing my own  path  whatever the words the implication is  often the same  who Do You Think You Are  in other words who are you to sidestep  expectation while the rest of us  contribute  [Music]  I sunk a lot of energy into trying to  safeguard myself from these sort of  questions  I worked hard for good grades I put  myself through college I even subscribed  to the corporate life  partly for myself  but also because I thought that's what  life expected of me but it didn't take  long to realize the expectations didn't  end there because once you have the  degree and the job and the car you're  expected to have the marriage and the  house and then the kids and on and on it  goes  until one day you pause long enough to  ask yourself  is any of this actually what I want  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  was this  Mr friends  I think careers are a 20th century  invention and I don't want one  you don't need to worry about me  I have a college education I'm not  destitute  I'm living like this by choice  I didn't know that kind of response was  even an option at 23.  everyone I knew was following the script  myself included  and it's not as if I abandoned that  script right away  the shifts were subtle and there were  plenty of detours along the way  [Music]  but over time those words inspired me to  find my own path Into the Wild  [Music]  onto the road  and to build a life I love  [Applause]  one step at a time  it's hard to say where I would be now  without that book  it prompted a massive shift in my  everything  in the best possible way  one thing is for sure though  I probably wouldn't be 37 single living  in a van down by the river  and man wouldn't that be sad  [Music]  thank you for being here  and I will see you all in the next one  you're biting my foot bro I should have  [ __ ] unbuckled this first I need a  mosquito soup  it's so bad right here  thank you

